cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ChemPotPy, cite both the ChemPotPy paper and the original
  publication for every potential energy surface used in your work.
title: ChemPotPy
abstract: >-
  A self-contained Python and modern Fortran library of analytic potential
  energy surfaces, diabatic potential energy matrices, gradients, and
  nonadiabatic couplings for molecular simulations.
type: software
